<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nugaal Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nugaal Valley is a long valley in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> running south-east from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sool">Sool</a> region to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> near Eyl. Seasonal water and grazing make it important to pastoral clans. At the turn of the 20th century it was a stronghold of the Dervish movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-abdullah-hassan">Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</a>, and today it lies largely within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puntland">Puntland</a>, whose capital Garowe stands in it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nugaal-valley.jpg" alt="Nugaal Valley" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 26oo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nugaal_Valley_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
